arm64-darwin  cxx1 keeps a cleanup region for `main` - `GCC_except_table.main` and the `__Unwind_Resume` it ends in - where clang's Darwin output has no exception table at all: it elides every temporary in this file and has nothing left to destroy on an unwind. Both are legal, elision being permitted rather than required in C++11, and cxx1 is the conservative side of the difference. The two Itanium name lists agree otherwise, and x86_64-linux and x86_64-windows agree on every name.
